<Base title="About | Fate Apothecary" description="About Fate Apothecary — practical food, herbs, gardening, and everyday wellness.">
  <article class="about-page shell">
    <header class="about-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">About Fate Apothecary</p>
      <h1>Food, herbs, growing, and a little intuition.</h1>
      <p class="about-lede">Fate Apothecary started with herbs and the idea that the things we grow, cook, and keep around us can be useful, nourishing, comforting, and worth understanding.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="about-copy">
      <p>It started as an herbal-medicine idea, but the bigger picture was always there: taking care of our bodies and the people we love in practical, everyday ways.</p>
      <p>I love to cook, but I am not a precise cook. I rarely measure unless it actually matters. I taste, adjust, substitute, use what I have, and frequently claim that my ancestors tell me when to stop adding ingredients.</p>
      <p>I also grow things, use herbs constantly, pay attention to what works for my own body, and keep learning. Fate Apothecary is where all of that gets collected: recipes, herb guides, garden notes, kitchen basics, and whatever else proves useful enough to share.</p>
      <p>The goal is not to tell you there is one perfect way to eat, grow, or live. It is to give you practical information, help you understand what you are working with, and make taking care of yourself feel a little less complicated.</p>
    </div>

    <aside class="about-note">
      <p class="eyebrow">One important note</p>
      <p>Fate Apothecary shares food, gardening, and traditional herbal knowledge for general informational purposes. Nothing here is a substitute for individualized medical advice.</p>
    </aside>
  </article>
</Base>
